Finger

finger://host/user asks host about user (RFC 1288) and shows the answer
as text; finger://host/ asks about everyone. Try finger://graph.no/oslo.

It shows the least a protocol Plug-In needs: PlugInNew fills in Mill's
MillInfo and the Plug-In's own tables, and the request method opens a
TCP connection with Mill's TcpOpen, writes an HTTP reply with Write, and
copies what the server sends.

KIT-BEGIN-REPO-ONLY
Finger.r is for Retro68 only: it puts the flat code Retro68 makes into
the 'MPlg' resource. MPW and CodeWarrior write that resource themselves.
